    "description": "Tests coding agents on long-horizon vulnerability discovery: given a disclosed bug report, produce a working proof-of-concept for Chromium V8, Mozilla SpiderMonkey, or the Linux kernel. An LLM judge checks that the PoC hits the intended bug rather than an unrelated crash. Related to, but distinct from, the earlier SEC-bench CVE PoC and patching suite.",
